    <section id="count">
      <h2>How to count your invoices</h2>
      <p>Your yearly invoice fee depends on how many invoices you send, so a good estimate saves money.</p>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Count:</b> sales invoices and credit notes you send to businesses and government.</li>
        <li><b>Don't count:</b> invoices you receive from suppliers. They are free in our fee. (Some providers count received documents too, which can double your count. Ask before you sign.)</li>
        <li><b>Don't count:</b> sales to consumers (B2C). They are outside e-invoicing for now.</li>
        <li><b>Quick way:</b> look at the invoice numbers you issued last year. The last number minus the first number is your yearly count. Or take one busy month and multiply by 12.</li>
        <li><b>Growing?</b> Add 10–20%. With exact pricing, if you send fewer invoices than you planned, your next year's fee goes down.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="hidden">
      <h2>Hidden costs to budget for</h2>
      <p>These are the costs that surprise business owners. Plan for them before you choose a provider.</p>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>A higher software plan.</b> Zoho Books needs Professional or higher. Free and Standard plans do not include e-invoicing.</li>
        <li><b>Keeping a subscription active.</b> TallyPrime e-invoicing stops working if TSS lapses.</li>
        <li><b>Data clean-up.</b> Every business customer needs a correct TRN, every item a VAT code, and addresses must be complete. Missing data is a common reason invoices get rejected. We include this in our setup.</li>
        <li><b>Old QuickBooks Desktop versions.</b> Some older versions cannot be connected. We check your version first.</li>
        <li><b>A computer that stays on.</b> With QuickBooks Desktop, invoices go out only while the QuickBooks computer is on and online.</li>
        <li><b>Received documents counted.</b> Some providers count supplier invoices as well as your sales invoices.</li>
        <li><b>Pack expiry and overage.</b> Some providers sell yearly packs that expire, and charge extra once a pack runs out.</li>
        <li><b>Support.</b> Some providers charge extra for WhatsApp or phone support, or reply by email only.</li>
        <li><b>Several companies.</b> Each company (TRN) is appointed and set up separately.</li>
        <li><b>Staff time.</b> Rejected invoices must be fixed and resent. We fix rejected invoices for you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

