    <section id="models">
      <h2>How e-invoicing pricing works in the market</h2>
      <p>Providers price e-invoicing in different ways, which makes comparing hard. These are the common models:</p>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Slabs or packs.</b> You buy a block of invoices (for example 1,000 or 5,000) for the year. If you send 1,100, you pay for the next block.</li>
        <li><b>Licence per company.</b> A monthly or yearly fee for each company (TRN), plus document packs on top.</li>
        <li><b>Built into the software.</b> Zoho Books, TallyPrime and Wafeq include e-invoicing in the software, sometimes with packs.</li>
        <li><b>Exact per invoice (our model).</b> A fixed fee covers your first {N0} invoices, then you pay for each invoice you actually send.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="sm">7 questions to ask any provider</h3>
      <ol class="olist">
        <li>Are you on the Ministry of Finance list of accredited service providers, or do you resell one?</li>
        <li>What do I pay in total in the first year, and every year after?</li>
        <li>Do you count invoices I receive, or only invoices I send?</li>
        <li>What happens if I send more invoices than my pack? Do unused invoices expire?</li>
        <li>Is connecting my software included, or extra?</li>
        <li>Who fixes rejected invoices, and how fast do you reply?</li>
        <li>Does the contract renew automatically, and how much notice do I need to cancel?</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="switch">
      <h2>Keep your software or switch?</h2>
      <p>Moving to Zoho Books, TallyPrime or Wafeq lowers the yearly e-invoicing cost, because they have it built in. But switching has its own costs: moving your data, retraining staff and changing how you work.</p>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table class="w700"><thead><tr><th>Software</th><th>Year 1</th><th>Year 2</th><th>Year 3</th><th>3-year total (our fees)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
